Support ticket #4482 (warehouse-west, overnight batch job):

"We batch-process overnight orders for warehouse-west. Almost every night,
somewhere in the middle-to-end of the batch, one order crashes the whole
run with a 'computed total is negative' error and we have to restart from
the last checkpoint. It's never the same order number twice - it depends
on how many orders are in that night's batch and how big they are. Small
test batches never reproduce it; bigger batches fail sooner. The crash
is in pricing.py, but the order that fails (ORD-1021 last night) looks
completely normal by itself: 3 items, $49 subtotal, nothing unusual. Please
find the actual bug - we don't think it's really about that one order."
